    "integration": "web 193 pass / testkit 57 pass / mobile 20 pass (single-worker); full suite 0 failures attributable to this port, 0 x 429 (was 262 x 429 before the rate-limit fix).",
    "rate_limit_resolution": {
      "problem": "Pre-existing: the spawned test API server capped auth at 200 req/IP with TRUST_PROXY off, so every test sign-up collapsed onto the shared 127.0.0.1 Redis bucket; a full suite poisoned it (~30min TTL) -> 262 x 429. Surfaced only by running the full local suite (repo default is affected-only).",
      "fix": "Enable TRUST_PROXY + give each testkit factory request a unique synthetic x-forwarded-for, AND raise the harness AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_*_MAX_REQUESTS to 1,000,000 (the documented \"effectively disabled\" intent; gated throttle tests drive their own limits). Browser-driven sign-ups (no x-forwarded-for) are covered by the high ceiling.",
      "verified": "262 x 429 -> 0 x 429."
    },
    "preexisting_failures_not_caused_by_port": [
      "apps/mobile: EADDRINUSE:4106 port-allocation race under file parallelism (rotates across mobile files). Reproduces identically on main. Out of scope for this infra port."
